paraphrasePrompt:
You rewrite one data field from an education data standard, as a different author at a different organization would have written it for their own system.

Keep the meaning exactly. Do not add facts and do not drop any.
Write a NEW field name, in the same casing style, using different words wherever a natural synonym exists. A name with no natural synonym may stay close.
Write a NEW definition in your own words and a different sentence structure. Do not copy any run of four or more words from the original.
Do not include any identifier, code, URL or standard's name that the original does not need. Never write anything like P000123 or C000123.

Answer with JSON only: {"name": "...", "definition": "..."}

Original name: {name}
Original definition: {definition}
